.policy "ruff-pyi032-any-eq-ne-annotation" revision 2
.description "Use object instead of Any to annotate the other operand of equality and inequality methods; object accepts every value while keeping type checking on."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI032 (flake8-pyi), every file: `__eq__` or `__ne__` in a class, with exactly two ordinary positional
// parameters (positional-only ones, before `/`, do not count), the second annotated `Any`. Equality accepts any
// object; `object` says so and keeps type checking on. Reported at the annotation.
//   def __eq__(self, other: Any) -> bool: ...     ← PYI032: write `other: object`
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI032(at: node) code "PYI032" "Annotate the other operand of this `__eq__` or `__ne__` as `object` instead of `Any`; `==` and `!=` must accept any value, and `Any` turns type checking off."
    suppress ruff "PYI032"
PYI032(a) :- pyi_method(_, f, x), (x = "__eq__" ; x = "__ne__"), count : { sig_param(f, p, n, i, "pos", b, d) } = 2,
    sig_param(f, _, _, j, "pos", a, _), count : { sig_param(f, p, n, i, "pos", b, d), i < j } = 1, !unset(a),
    type_bare(a, t), typing_sym(t, "Any").
